<title>FRANCE: BMW, Chrysler in Latam engine venture.</title>
<headline>BMW, Chrysler in Latam engine venture.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. carmaker Chrysler and German carmaker BMW said on Tuesday they would set up a joint venture to build four-cylinder engines in Latin America, investing $400-500 million.</p>
<p>The joint venture will produce about 400,000 units per year, half of them for BMW and half for Chrysler, the chairmen of the two firms told a joint news conference at the Paris car show.</p>
<p>Chrysler chairman Bob Eaton said that the precise location would be decided by the end of the year and that the venture would produce 1.4 and 1.6 litre engines.</p>
</text>
